  "scope": "A temporary Kind pod stores an owned synthetic vector index in SQLite on a PVC. The case creates a versioned approved snapshot and a benign altered snapshot, observes an unsafe activation fail the known-vector query, then verifies activation blocking against separately mounted approved metadata while preserving the live index. The snapshot persists across Pod replacement. It performs an approved-source rebuild and known-query check, unlinks one named retired fixture generation, then restores the approved snapshot after replacing the primary PVC from a second case-owned PVC in the same cluster. A fifth bounded check rejects an incompatible model/dimension request without changing the restored bytes, then validates a separately pinned migration plan's staged SQLite output and known query before activation.",
